Date: Sun, 26 Apr 2026 17:28:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] Items 18-20: PreparedGeometry, transform callbacks, P2
 fillers

Item 18 - GEOSPreparedGeometry
  Factory: GEOSGeometry::prepare() -> GEOSPreparedGeometry
  17 methods: contains, containsProperly, containsXY, coveredBy,
              covers, crosses, disjoint, intersects, intersectsXY,
              overlaps, touches, within, relate, relatePattern,
              distance, distanceWithin, nearestPoints
  __construct() locked.

  Lifecycle: PreparedRelay struct holds GEOSPreparedGeometry* +
  ZVAL_COPY of source GEOSGeometry zval. Source is kept alive for
  the prepared geom's lifetime. Dtor destroys prepared first,
  then drops source zval refcount.

Item 19 - Coordinate-transform callbacks
  GEOSGeometry::transformXY(callable) -> GEOSGeometry
  GEOSGeometry::transformXYZ(callable) -> GEOSGeometry

  PHP callable receives ($x, $y[, $z]), returns
  [$newX, $newY[, $newZ]]. Sticky-exception capture mirrors
  STRtree pattern. Validates ret-array shape and applies numeric
  coercion before writing back to GEOS.

Item 20 - P2 fillers
  GEOSGeometry::hilbertCode($extent, $level) : int
  GEOSGeometry::gridIntersectionFractions($xmin, $ymin, $xmax,
                                          $ymax, $nx, $ny) : array
                (signature follows C API; plan's '$grid geometry'
                form would need a PHP-side wrapper)
  Standalone GEOSOrientationIndex($ax, $ay, $bx, $by, $px, $py)
  Standalone GEOSSegmentIntersection(8 doubles) : ?array

Tests: 040_PreparedGeometry.phpt, 050_Transform.phpt, 060_Misc.phpt.

25/25 .phpt tests pass.
